{"title":"Career Roadmap · Epigraphy Assistant","role":"Epigraphy Assistant","summary":"An Epigraphy Assistant supports the study, documentation, preservation and interpretation of historical inscriptions found on:","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Level","Education","Category","Degree / Programme","Specialisation","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Undergraduate"},{"text":"Humanities & Social Sciences"},{"text":"BA (General / Honours)"},{"text":"Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology"},{"text":"Epigraphy Assistant"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Epigraphy Assistant supports the study, documentation, preservation and interpretation of historical inscriptions found on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stone monuments"},{"text":"Temple walls"},{"text":"Copper plates"},{"text":"Coins"},{"text":"Pillars"},{"text":"Seals"},{"text":"Sculptures"},{"text":"Manuscripts and other historical artefacts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Epigraphy is particularly valuable for reconstructing information about political history, administration, religion, land grants, social institutions, languages, scripts, trade and cultural development."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology is a very strong academic foundation for this pathway."},{"type":"p","text":"However, professional epigraphy is a specialised research field. A BA can support assistant, research-support, documentation and heritage roles, while advanced research and specialist positions commonly benefit from postgraduate study in Ancient History, Archaeology, Epigraphy, Sanskrit, History, Museology or related fields."}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Aspect","Reality"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree alignment"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Direct entry"},{"text":"Possible for assistant/support roles"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Highly specialised"}],[{"text":"Sanskrit/classical-language knowledge"},{"text":"Very valuable"}],[{"text":"Script knowledge"},{"text":"Critical for advanced work"}],[{"text":"Research skills"},{"text":"Critical"}],[{"text":"Fieldwork"},{"text":"Important"}],[{"text":"Digital skills"},{"text":"Increasingly important"}],[{"text":"PG requirement"},{"text":"Strongly recommended for advanced roles"}],[{"text":"Government heritage opportunities"},{"text":"Notification-specific"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Important distinction"},{"type":"p","text":"An Epigraphy Assistant supports researchers and heritage professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"A senior Epigraphist may independently:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Read ancient inscriptions"},{"text":"Identify scripts"},{"text":"Transcribe texts"},{"text":"Translate them"},{"text":"Date inscriptions"},{"text":"Interpret historical context"},{"text":"Publish scholarly research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"That level of expertise generally requires much deeper language, script and research training."}]},{"heading":"What Does an Epigraphy Assistant Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the institution, responsibilities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Locating inscriptions"},{"text":"Recording inscriptions"},{"text":"Photographing monuments"},{"text":"Creating documentation"},{"text":"Transcribing inscriptional text"},{"text":"Assisting with translations"},{"text":"Recording script characteristics"},{"text":"Creating inscription databases"},{"text":"Maintaining metadata"},{"text":"Supporting archaeological fieldwork"},{"text":"Assisting researchers"},{"text":"Preparing bibliographies"},{"text":"Comparing inscriptions"},{"text":"Digitising historical records"},{"text":"Creating GIS records"},{"text":"Maintaining archival material"},{"text":"Supporting museum/heritage documentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Major Areas of Knowledge","kind":"ot